Bugfix: Fall back to the first trusted domain whatever its array key

When a request arrived with an untrusted Host header, the server fell back to
`$trusted_domains[0]`. After entries were removed from config.php the list can
look like `[2 => 'cloud.example.com']`; index 0 then did not exist, the server
host became null (with an "Undefined array key 0" warning) and the request
failed further down. The first configured entry is now used regardless of its
key. A `trusted_domains` value that is not a list is treated as not set, as the
trusted domain check already did, instead of returning its first character.
